  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening the resilience of Indigenous and tribal Peoples` food and knowledge systems through access to social protection.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The sub-programme aims at informing global policy design on strengthening the resilience of Indigenous and tribal Peoples in the context of climate risks and biodiversity loss, with particular focus on Indigenous Peoples? food and knowledge systems and the role of social protection programmes in enhancing their resilience.
The sub-programme will review national policies across the HDP Nexus and their implementation in the context of ongoing agrifood programmes technically assisted by FAO in target countries to identify and better understand i) social protection design elements and ongoing good practices for the inclusion of Indigenous and tribal Peoples and for strengthening the resilience of their food and knowledge systems ; ii) opportunities to better access these programmes; and if relevant iii) Indigenous and tribal Peoples contributions that can add value to social protection as part of programmes to enhance the resilience of their food and knowledge systems in the face of multiple shocks and stresses.
In doing so the sub-programme will directly consult Indigenous and tribal Peoples to assess the profile of their food and knowledge systems, their access to opportunities, services (with a focus on social protection programmes) and markets. Thus, the sub-programme will support global exchange of knowledge and policy dialogue on the key role that Indigenous and tribal People</narrative>
  </description>
